# Static stack gate for the ESP32-H2/C6 ZRHP NCP images (examples/esp32-ncp).
# Usage: tools/esp32-ncp-stack-gate.py ELF @tools/esp32-ncp-stack-gate.args
#
# Heuristic direct-call bound, not a whole-program proof: indirect calls
# other than the log sink and the interrupt handlers are not followed. The
# hardware stack paint stays the authoritative runtime evidence.

# esp-hal: the main stack is all RAM above .bss/.noinit; the stack-guard word
# (ESP_HAL_CONFIG_STACK_GUARD_OFFSET = 60, watchpoint-monitored) ends the
# usable stack 64 B above `_stack_end_cpu0`.
--guard
64

# H2 USJ fix build (ncp-capacity, 256 TC devices): 56 096 B usable; static
# worst case 34 112 B task (boot composition: device assembly) + 512 B log
# sink + 864 B interrupts = 35 488 B, a 20 608 B gap. H2 Thread-BR: 53 512 B
# usable, 1 104 B interrupts, a 17 784 B gap. C6: 245 440 B usable. Not
# measured on hardware.
--min-gap
16384

# Frames above 12 KiB must be reviewed. Ncp::new_into (inlined into the
# example's `new_ncp` boot step) still builds the ZRHP link engine
# (22.5 KiB) by value: boot only, beside the deeper composition.
--max-frame
12288
--frame-allow
esp32_ncp::new_ncp=23552

# Task context: `main` reaches the composition steps and, through the
# executor, the root future's polls by direct calls. Every `log!` reaches the
# ring logger through `dyn Log`.
--entry
^main$
--task-extra
RingLogger as log::Log>::log$

# Interrupts: `_start_TrapN_trap` reserves a 64 B frame, `handle_interrupts`
# dispatches through the vector table with interrupts re-enabled (a higher
# priority nests), so every bound #[handler] counts once. The radio handler
# reaches the MAC completion callbacks through pointers.
--trap-frame
64
--irq-dispatch
^handle_interrupts$
--irq-handler
::__esp_hal_internal_
--irq-callback
^zigbee_mac::esp::radio_phy::on_
# The trap entry switches to a reserved stack on overflow (exception path).
--dynamic-allow
^_pre_default_start_trap$

# Chain budgets: worst depth below (and including) any matching function,
# measured on the fix build, rounded up to the next 512 B. A regression fails.
--chain-budget
boot=^esp32_ncp::compose$=33280
--chain-budget
serve=^esp32_ncp::serve$=29696
# Trust Center: initialization, the step's TC service and persistence. Before
# the in-place state fix these were 485-576 KiB (whole-state clones).
--chain-budget
trust-center=TrustCenterCoordinatorApp<.*>>::(step_deferred_factory_reset|ensure_trust_center_initialized|service_network_key_rotation)::?=16384
--chain-budget
tc-runtime=^<zigbee_runtime::trust_center_runtime::TrustCenterRuntime<=9728
--chain-budget
tc-journal=TrustCenterStreamJournal<.*>>::(load_into|store|frame_snapshot|decode_snapshot|newest_framed)$=9216
